# Lab Sheet 5 - Question 10: Configure Apache .htaccess files and handler directives to execute Python scripts seamlessly within web directories.

# Place this .htaccess inside the web directory containing .py scripts
# e.g. C:/xampp/htdocs/pyapp/.htaccess

Options +ExecCGI
AddHandler cgi-script .py
DirectoryIndex index.py index.html

# Optional: show clean URLs without extension (needs mod_rewrite)
# RewriteEngine On
# RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME}.py -f
# RewriteRule ^(.*)$ $1.py [L]

# ---- Requirements ----
# 1. httpd.conf: the directory must allow overrides:
#      <Directory "C:/xampp/htdocs/pyapp">
#          AllowOverride All
#      </Directory>
# 2. mod_cgi (and mod_rewrite) enabled; restart Apache.
# 3. Scripts need the shebang line (#!C:/Python311/python.exe or #!/usr/bin/env python3),
#    print("Content-Type: text/html\n") first, and chmod +x on Linux.
# 4. Test: create test.py in the folder and open http://localhost/pyapp/test.py
